#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0119 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "THE OPPOSITE EFFECT TO CG0118's, and the reason the two must not share a fixture. CG0119 fires WHEN ACTARM is reserved and differs from ARM, so recognising the CT casing makes it fire MORE. Row 2 is 'SCREEN FAILURE' against ARM='Placebo' - invisible before upper(), a violation after."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-2
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=01-002
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ARM      type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
col ACTARM   type=Char label="Description of Actual Arm"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-001 | Placebo | Placebo
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-002 | Placebo | SCREEN FAILURE
---
